{"id":"08","title":"Saying Thank You","goal":"Thank someone for a specific action, respond to thanks, and distinguish gratitude from a literal request or a frustrated reaction.","language":"en","study":[{"id":"08-study-0","title":"Name what you appreciate","blocks":[{"id":"ch08-b0","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"Thanks","emphasis":true},{"text":" is a short expression of gratitude. "},{"text":"Thank you","emphasis":true},{"text":" is another choice. You can add the reason:"}],"span":[6,6],"phraseIds":["ch08-p64466082672555","ch08-p167252145005773"]},{"id":"ch08-b1","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"number":null,"runs":[{"text":"Thanks for your help.","emphasis":true},{"text":" Thank someone for helping."}],"phraseIds":["ch08-p119882666982005"]},{"number":null,"runs":[{"text":"Thank you for waiting.","emphasis":true},{"text":" Thank someone for the action of waiting."}],"phraseIds":["ch08-p90432578889427"]},{"number":null,"runs":[{"text":"Thanks for the ride.","emphasis":true},{"text":" Thank someone for taking you somewhere."}],"phraseIds":["ch08-p116787530686140"]},{"number":null,"runs":[{"text":"Thanks for having me over.","emphasis":true},{"text":" Thank a host for inviting you to their home."}],"phraseIds":["ch08-p54279783209356"]},{"number":null,"runs":[{"text":"I really appreciate it.","emphasis":true},{"text":" Emphasize that their action matters to you."}],"phraseIds":["ch08-p179931412198999"]}],"span":[8,12],"phraseIds":["ch08-p119882666982005","ch08-p90432578889427","ch08-p116787530686140","ch08-p54279783209356","ch08-p179931412198999"]},{"id":"ch08-b2","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"After "},{"text":"for","emphasis":true},{"text":", use the thing or action: "},{"text":"for your help","emphasis":true},{"text":", "},{"text":"for waiting","emphasis":true},{"text":". You do not need a long explanation for every small favor."}],"span":[14,14],"phraseIds":["ch08-p194629025143029","ch08-p228565589136638","ch08-p11052468175957"]},{"id":"ch08-b3","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"A practical favor","emphasis":true}],"span":[16,16],"phraseIds":[]},{"id":"ch08-b4","type":"conversation","turns":[{"speaker":"Leah","runs":[{"text":"Here's the umbrella you can borrow."}],"id":"ch08-line18","person":"Leah","en":"Here's the umbrella you can borrow.","ja":"","portrait":"portrait-8828935.svg"},{"speaker":"Owen","runs":[{"text":"Thanks. I really appreciate it."}],"id":"ch08-line19","person":"Owen","en":"Thanks. I really appreciate it.","ja":"","portrait":"portrait-8935736.svg"},{"speaker":"Leah","runs":[{"text":"No problem."}],"id":"ch08-line20","person":"Leah","en":"No problem.","ja":"","portrait":"portrait-8828935.svg"},{"speaker":"Owen","runs":[{"text":"I'll bring it back tomorrow."}],"id":"ch08-line21","person":"Owen","en":"I'll bring it back tomorrow.","ja":"","portrait":"portrait-8935736.svg"}],"span":[18,21],"art":"ch08-scene-0.svg","theme":"thanks","people":["Leah","Owen"],"caption":"Name what you appreciate · Leah & Owen","phraseIds":["ch08-line18","ch08-line19","ch08-line20","ch08-line21"]},{"id":"ch08-b5","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"Returning a borrowed object is part of this particular scene, not something every thank-you exchange needs. "},{"text":"Thank you so much","emphasis":true},{"text":" and "},{"text":"I can't thank you enough","emphasis":true},{"text":" can express stronger gratitude when that is what you mean."}],"span":[23,23],"phraseIds":["ch08-p30115042638947","ch08-p203746801522921"]}],"line":4,"ja":"","theme":"thanks"},{"id":"08-study-1","title":"Respond to thanks","blocks":[{"id":"ch08-b6","type":"table","header":[[{"text":"Reply"}],[{"text":"A possible use"}]],"rows":[[[{"text":"You're welcome.","emphasis":true}],[{"text":"Acknowledge the thanks."}]],[[{"text":"No problem.","emphasis":true}],[{"text":"Present the help as something you were happy to do."}]],[[{"text":"Happy to help.","emphasis":true}],[{"text":"Explicitly express willingness to help."}]],[[{"text":"My pleasure.","emphasis":true}],[{"text":"Say you enjoyed providing the help or hospitality."}]],[[{"text":"Anytime.","emphasis":true}],[{"text":"Offer an informal sense of willingness to help again."}]]],"span":[27,33],"phraseIds":["ch08-p6147576973999","ch08-p29280373687464","ch08-p225538616964965","ch08-p159281981972302","ch08-p41128090047414"],"phraseCells":[["ch08-p6147576973999",null],["ch08-p29280373687464",null],["ch08-p225538616964965",null],["ch08-p159281981972302",null],["ch08-p41128090047414",null]]},{"id":"ch08-b7","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"After dinner at a friend's home","emphasis":true}],"span":[35,35],"phraseIds":[]},{"id":"ch08-b8","type":"conversation","turns":[{"speaker":"Owen","runs":[{"text":"Thanks for having me over. Dinner was great."}],"id":"ch08-line37","person":"Owen","en":"Thanks for having me over. Dinner was great.","ja":"","portrait":"portrait-8935736.svg"},{"speaker":"Leah","runs":[{"text":"You're welcome. It was good to see you."}],"id":"ch08-line38","person":"Leah","en":"You're welcome. It was good to see you.","ja":"","portrait":"portrait-8828935.svg"},{"speaker":"Owen","runs":[{"text":"I had a really nice evening."}],"id":"ch08-line39","person":"Owen","en":"I had a really nice evening.","ja":"","portrait":"portrait-8935736.svg"}],"span":[37,39],"art":"ch08-scene-1.svg","theme":"thanks","people":["Owen","Leah"],"caption":"Respond to thanks · Owen & Leah","phraseIds":["ch08-line37","ch08-line38","ch08-line39"]},{"id":"ch08-b9","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"Anytime","emphasis":true},{"text":" can sound welcoming, but it does not have to be an unlimited promise of availability. "},{"text":"No problem","emphasis":true},{"text":" is a recognized response to thanks; do not assume it rejects the gratitude. The same words can reassure someone after an apology in Chapter 9."}],"span":[41,41],"phraseIds":["ch08-p37495934424444","ch08-p120512474143832"]}],"line":25,"ja":"","theme":"thanks"},{"id":"08-study-2","title":"Gifts and compliments","blocks":[{"id":"ch08-b10","type":"conversation","turns":[{"speaker":"Leah","runs":[{"text":"I brought you a small birthday gift."}],"id":"ch08-line45","person":"Leah","en":"I brought you a small birthday gift.","ja":"","portrait":"portrait-8828935.svg"},{"speaker":"Owen","runs":[{"text":"Oh, wow. You shouldn't have! Thank you."}],"id":"ch08-line46","person":"Owen","en":"Oh, wow. You shouldn't have! Thank you.","ja":"","portrait":"portrait-8935736.svg"},{"speaker":"Leah","runs":[{"text":"I thought you might like it."}],"id":"ch08-line47","person":"Leah","en":"I thought you might like it.","ja":"","portrait":"portrait-8828935.svg"}],"span":[45,47],"art":"ch08-scene-2.svg","theme":"thanks","people":["Leah","Owen"],"caption":"Gifts and compliments · Leah & Owen","phraseIds":["ch08-line45","ch08-line46","ch08-line47"]},{"id":"ch08-b11","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"In this gift exchange, "},{"text":"You shouldn't have","emphasis":true},{"text":" expresses surprise and appreciation, not a demand to take the gift away. If you really want to refuse a gift, say that clearly rather than relying on this expression."}],"span":[49,49],"phraseIds":["ch08-p100586917243826"]},{"id":"ch08-b12","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"After a compliment, you can accept it:"}],"span":[51,51],"phraseIds":[]},{"id":"ch08-b13","type":"conversation","turns":[{"speaker":"Leah","runs":[{"text":"Your presentation was really clear."}],"id":"ch08-line53","person":"Leah","en":"Your presentation was really clear.","ja":"","portrait":"portrait-8828935.svg"},{"speaker":"Owen","runs":[{"text":"Thank you. I appreciate that."}],"id":"ch08-line54","person":"Owen","en":"Thank you. I appreciate that.","ja":"","portrait":"portrait-8935736.svg"}],"span":[53,54],"art":"ch08-scene-3.svg","theme":"thanks","people":["Leah","Owen"],"caption":"Gifts and compliments · Leah & Owen","phraseIds":["ch08-line53","ch08-line54"]},{"id":"ch08-b14","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"You can give a sincere compliment in return, but you do not have to invent one. "},{"text":"I owe you one","emphasis":true},{"text":" informally acknowledges a favor and suggests returning the favor; it is optional here."}],"span":[56,56],"phraseIds":["ch08-p235493614998293"]}],"line":43,"ja":"","theme":"thanks"},{"id":"08-study-3","title":"Optional: The same words, a different intention","blocks":[{"id":"ch08-b15","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"Thanks a lot","emphasis":true},{"text":" can be sincere. In an explicitly frustrated exchange—"},{"text":"You left without telling me? Thanks a lot","emphasis":true},{"text":"—it can express annoyance instead. The event and delivery change the interpretation. Use a clear "},{"text":"I'm upset that you left without telling me","emphasis":true},{"text":" if you want the complaint to be unmistakable."}],"span":[60,60],"phraseIds":["ch08-p58543491598040","ch08-p8864887277601","ch08-p208750873144422"]}],"line":58,"ja":"","theme":"thanks"},{"id":"08-words","title":"Words & phrases","blocks":[{"id":"08-glossary","type":"vocabulary","phraseIds":["ch08-v0","ch08-v1","ch08-v2","ch08-v3"]}]}],"practice":[{"id":"08-practice-0","title":"Make the gratitude specific","blocks":[{"id":"ch08-b16","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"Use the complete scene facts below. Practice both people aloud on your own. Start with the models, then cover them."}],"span":[64,64]},{"id":"ch08-b17","type":"list","ordered":true,"items":[{"number":1,"runs":[{"text":"A friend held the door while you carried a heavy bag. Thank them. They answer "},{"text":"You're welcome","emphasis":true},{"text":". Finish the brief exchange if needed."}],"id":"ch08-b17-0"},{"number":2,"runs":[{"text":"A colleague waited ten minutes for you. Thank them specifically for waiting. They reply "},{"text":"No problem","emphasis":true},{"text":"."}],"id":"ch08-b17-1"},{"number":3,"runs":[{"text":"You are leaving Leah's home after dinner. Thank her for the invitation and say one positive thing about the evening. Support: "},{"text":"Dinner was great","emphasis":true},{"text":", "},{"text":"I had a nice evening","emphasis":true},{"text":"."}],"id":"ch08-b17-2"},{"number":4,"runs":[{"text":"Someone praises your drawing: "},{"text":"I love the colors","emphasis":true},{"text":". Accept the compliment without being required to praise something back."}],"id":"ch08-b17-3"},{"number":5,"runs":[{"text":"Your friend helped you move furniture. Give a stronger thank-you. As the friend, acknowledge it with one of the response choices."}],"id":"ch08-b17-4"},{"number":6,"runs":[{"text":"Compare two scenes: a friend patiently waited for you; a different friend left without telling you and you were left waiting. Try a sincere "},{"text":"Thanks for waiting","emphasis":true},{"text":" in the first scene and a sarcastic "},{"text":"Thanks a lot","emphasis":true},{"text":" in the second. Explain what each communicates. For the second scene, you can choose the direct complaint instead."}],"id":"ch08-b17-5"},{"number":7,"runs":[{"text":"Hide Study. Thank someone for a real or invented favor and rehearse their acknowledgment. Change the favor on the second attempt."}],"id":"ch08-b17-6"}],"span":[66,72]}],"line":62,"ja":"","theme":"thanks","answers":[{"id":"ch08-b18","type":"answerHeading","runs":[{"text":"Sample possibilities"}],"span":[74,74]},{"id":"ch08-b19","type":"list","ordered":true,"items":[{"number":1,"runs":[{"text":"Thanks for holding the door. — You're welcome.","emphasis":true}]},{"number":2,"runs":[{"text":"Thank you for waiting. — No problem.","emphasis":true}]},{"number":3,"runs":[{"text":"Thanks for having me over. Dinner was great. — My pleasure.","emphasis":true}]},{"number":4,"runs":[{"text":"Thank you. I appreciate that.","emphasis":true}]},{"number":5,"runs":[{"text":"Thank you so much for your help. — Happy to help.","emphasis":true}]},{"number":6,"runs":[{"text":"The first expresses gratitude for patience. The second can express frustration in the stated scene, although the words alone do not guarantee sarcasm."}]}],"span":[76,81]},{"id":"ch08-b20","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"Check:","emphasis":true},{"text":" Did you identify what you appreciate? Did the acknowledgment fit? If your intention was a complaint, would the other person understand that from the context or clearer wording?"}],"span":[83,83]}]}],"phrases":[{"id":"ch08-p64466082672555","en":"Thanks","section":"08-study-0","context":"Name what you appreciate","kind":"word","studyId":"ch08-p64466082672555"},{"id":"ch08-p167252145005773","en":"Thank you","section":"08-study-0","context":"Name what you appreciate","kind":"word","studyId":"ch08-p167252145005773"},{"id":"ch08-p119882666982005","en":"Thanks for your help.","section":"08-study-0","context":"Name what you appreciate","kind":"phrase","studyId":"ch08-p119882666982005"},{"id":"ch08-p90432578889427","en":"Thank you for waiting.","section":"08-study-0","context":"Name what you appreciate","kind":"phrase","studyId":"ch08-p90432578889427"},{"id":"ch08-p116787530686140","en":"Thanks for the ride.","section":"08-study-0","context":"Name what you appreciate","kind":"phrase","studyId":"ch08-p116787530686140"},{"id":"ch08-p54279783209356","en":"Thanks for having me over.","section":"08-study-0","context":"Name what you appreciate","kind":"phrase","studyId":"ch08-p54279783209356"},{"id":"ch08-p179931412198999","en":"I really appreciate it.","section":"08-study-0","context":"Name what you appreciate","kind":"phrase","studyId":"ch08-p179931412198999"},{"id":"ch08-p194629025143029","en":"for","section":"08-study-0","context":"Name what you appreciate","kind":"word","studyId":"ch08-p194629025143029"},{"id":"ch08-p228565589136638","en":"for your help","section":"08-study-0","context":"Name what you appreciate","kind":"phrase","studyId":"ch08-p228565589136638"},{"id":"ch08-p11052468175957","en":"for waiting","section":"08-study-0","context":"Name what you appreciate","kind":"word","studyId":"ch08-p11052468175957"},{"id":"ch08-line18","en":"Here's the umbrella you can borrow.","section":"08-study-0","context":"Leah · Name what you appreciate","kind":"phrase","speaker":"Leah","portrait":"portrait-8828935.svg","studyId":"ch08-line18"},{"id":"ch08-line19","en":"Thanks. I really appreciate it.","section":"08-study-0","context":"Owen · Name what you appreciate","kind":"phrase","speaker":"Owen","portrait":"portrait-8935736.svg","studyId":"ch08-line19"},{"id":"ch08-line20","en":"No problem.","section":"08-study-0","context":"Leah · Name what you appreciate","kind":"phrase","speaker":"Leah","portrait":"portrait-8828935.svg","studyId":"ch08-line20"},{"id":"ch08-line21","en":"I'll bring it back tomorrow.","section":"08-study-0","context":"Owen · Name what you appreciate","kind":"phrase","speaker":"Owen","portrait":"portrait-8935736.svg","studyId":"ch08-line21"},{"id":"ch08-p30115042638947","en":"Thank you so much","section":"08-study-0","context":"Name what you appreciate","kind":"phrase","studyId":"ch08-p30115042638947"},{"id":"ch08-p203746801522921","en":"I can't thank you enough","section":"08-study-0","context":"Name what you appreciate","kind":"phrase","studyId":"ch08-p203746801522921"},{"id":"ch08-p6147576973999","en":"You're welcome.","section":"08-study-1","context":"Acknowledge the thanks.","kind":"phrase","studyId":"ch08-p6147576973999"},{"id":"ch08-p29280373687464","en":"No problem.","section":"08-study-1","context":"Present the help as something you were happy to do.","kind":"phrase","studyId":"ch08-p29280373687464"},{"art":"word-support.svg","id":"ch08-p225538616964965","en":"Happy to help.","section":"08-study-1","context":"Explicitly express willingness to help.","kind":"phrase","studyId":"ch08-p225538616964965"},{"id":"ch08-p159281981972302","en":"My pleasure.","section":"08-study-1","context":"Say you enjoyed providing the help or hospitality.","kind":"phrase","studyId":"ch08-p159281981972302"},{"id":"ch08-p41128090047414","en":"Anytime.","section":"08-study-1","